"overall": "A faithful, literal rendering that keeps the Septuagintal obscurities (verses 13-17, 19b, 24) without smoothing them toward the Hebrew; no critical or major faults. The remaining points are small additions ('até', 'cabe', 'seja'), one number change (salutarium) and one imported Pauline idiom in 19a. The pointing marks match the Latin in every verse (one mediant each, (fit reverentia) kept); the embedded verse-number parentheticals of the Latin are omitted, which is not a pointing issue."}
